{"id":6190,"date":"2019-12-03T22:03:35","date_gmt":"2019-12-04T03:03:35","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/?p=6190"},"modified":"2019-12-03T22:03:35","modified_gmt":"2019-12-04T03:03:35","slug":"yellowstone","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/2019\/12\/03\/yellowstone\/","title":{"rendered":"Yellowstone"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p>I haven&#8217;t posted for the longest time and I&#8217;ve been feeling guilty about that.  I wanted to fill you in on what&#8217;s been going on and where we&#8217;ve been over the last couple of months.  The reason I haven&#8217;t posted is because we&#8217;ve had very limited wifi.  <\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Our Verizon Jet Pack has a 25 gig data per month limit, but now we&#8217;re using a new service that gives us UNLIMITED data for only $25\/month (more on that later) and so now we can post pictures and video without worrying about going over our data limit.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>We left our volunteer gig at D.C. Booth National Historic Fish Hatchery in Spearfish, SD on Sept 18th and made our way west to Yellowstone National Park for about a week.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>While there we camped about 20 miles east of the east entrance to Yellowstone at <a rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" aria-label=\"Wapiti (waapadee) Campground (opens in a new tab)\" href=\"https:\/\/www.fs.usda.gov\/recarea\/shoshone\/recreation\/camping-cabins\/recarea\/?recid=36267&amp;actid=29\" target=\"_blank\">Wapiti (waapadee) Campground<\/a> in the Shoshone National Forest.   It was a nice small (electric only) campground with about 40 sites and a host couple.  We were able to stay there for only $8 a night with our America The Beautiful Senior Pass.  We would like to have stayed right IN Yellowstone, but the campgrounds in the park were pretty full and a little tight for our 36&#8242; motorhome and we figured the 20 minute ride into the park was not a big inconvenience.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"760\" height=\"428\" src=\"https:\/\/i2.wp.com\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/11\/20190919_183317-scaled.jpg?fit=685%2C385&amp;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-6224\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/11\/20190919_183317-scaled.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/11\/20190919_183317-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/11\/20190919_183317-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/11\/20190919_183317-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/11\/20190919_183317-1536x864.jpg 1536w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/11\/20190919_183317-2048x1152.jpg 2048w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/11\/20190919_183317-685x385.jpg 685w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/11\/20190919_183317-2000x1125.jpg 2000w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-video\"><video height=\"1080\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 1920 \/ 1080;\" width=\"1920\" controls src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/11\/20190922_161629.mp4\"><\/video><figcaption>Our camp site at Wapiti Campground about 20 miles east of Yellowstone NP<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>We were planning on spending 8 days visiting Yellowstone and our first day was rainy and about 40 degrees.  We drove in through the drizzle in the morning and visited a few of the sites and then decided since we had a few more days to visit we&#8217;d head on back home to our site and try for better weather tomorrow.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Boy were we in for a surprise!  As we headed east toward the east gate, a Park Ranger was blocking the road and advised us that Sylvan Pass (10,000&#8242; elev.) was closed because &#8220;the plows can&#8217;t keep up with the snow&#8221;!  We had no choice but to turn around and either find a room in one of the parks two lodges or retreat out one of the 3 other park exits and make our way back to Wapiti.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>As it turned out, ultimately we had to go out the south entrance, through Jackson Hole and then head southeast through Dubois and Riverton and then back north through Thermopolis and Cody, then finally back to Wapiti Campground.  It was a 540 mile day &#8211; we left Yellowstone about 4 p.m. and got back to camp around 12:30 a.m. What a trip! <\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"760\" height=\"428\" src=\"https:\/\/i2.wp.com\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/11\/540MileTripMap-scaled.jpg?fit=685%2C385&amp;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-6228\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/11\/540MileTripMap-scaled.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/11\/540MileTripMap-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/11\/540MileTripMap-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/11\/540MileTripMap-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/11\/540MileTripMap-1536x864.jpg 1536w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/11\/540MileTripMap-2048x1152.jpg 2048w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/11\/540MileTripMap-685x385.jpg 685w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/11\/540MileTripMap-2000x1125.jpg 2000w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px\" \/><figcaption>Our 540 mile trip from YNP down to Riverton, up to Cody and back west to Wapiti<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed-youtube wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\n<iframe loading=\"lazy\" title=\"Escaping From Yellowstone\" width=\"685\" height=\"385\" src=\"https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/embed\/ZnG6Ych63RQ?feature=oembed\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen><\/iframe>\n<\/div><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>But subsequent days offered us a wonderful time seeing many of the &#8220;hot pots&#8221; including Old Faithful along with beautiful waterfalls and a few wild animals as well!<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped wp-block-gallery-1 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex\"><ul class=\"blocks-gallery-grid\"><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"720\" height=\"540\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/11\/IMG_2789-scaled.jpg?fit=685%2C514&amp;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" data-id=\"6230\" data-full-url=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/11\/IMG_2789-scaled.jpg?fit=2560%2C1920&amp;ssl=1\" data-link=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/?attachment_id=6230\" class=\"wp-image-6230\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/11\/IMG_2789-scaled.jpg 720w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/11\/IMG_2789-300x225.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/11\/IMG_2789-1024x768.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/11\/IMG_2789-768x576.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/11\/IMG_2789-1536x1152.jpg 1536w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/11\/IMG_2789-2048x1536.jpg 2048w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/11\/IMG_2789-685x514.jpg 685w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/11\/IMG_2789-2000x1500.jpg 2000w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 720px) 100vw, 720px\" \/><\/figure><\/li><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"720\" height=\"540\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/11\/IMG_2790-scaled.jpg?fit=685%2C514&amp;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" data-id=\"6231\"